{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And all his brothers I have given him for servants.</b> This is not the blessing of \"be a lord over your brothers,\" for he had already said, \"Behold, I have set him as a lord over you,\" but it is possible that he may be the lord yet they not be servants, as in the matter of \"for Judah prevailed over his brothers\" (I Chronicles 5:2). But he said, \"I have given him for servants,\" from his statement \"and let your mother's sons bow down to you\" (Genesis 27:29), for that is the bowing of a slave to his master, as he said, \"let peoples serve you\" and he repeats \"and let nations bow down to you.\" And the sense of \"and all his brothers\" is like the sense of \"your brothers\" and \"your mother's sons\" — he mentions them in plural language to hint at all the seed of Esau. And Rabbi Abraham said: the sons of the concubines."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Rabbi Abraham refers to Ibn Ezra, who interprets 'all his brothers' as the sons of Abraham's concubines (Keturah's offspring), whom Isaac had given to Jacob as servants."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:16.601655339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}